      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is twice the maximum, so it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day in total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
